#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048257 :topic/id #uuid "8cc35c33-61af-5ac3-971b-a33b8bbdcb9d" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124485 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124298 :question/id #uuid "a788a6e6-8fb4-5657-912d-2eb8295a297f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4800" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors $\\mathbf{v}_1, \\mathbf{v}_2, \\mathbf{v}_3 \\in V.$ Given that $\\{ \\mathbf{v}_1, \\mathbf{v}_2, \\mathbf{v}_3\\}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\{ 4\\mathbf{v}_1, 5\\mathbf{v}_2, \\mathbf{v}_3\\}$ is linearly independent\n\n- $\\{ \\mathbf{0}, \\mathbf{v}_1, 2\\mathbf{v}_2 \\}$ is linearly independent\n\n- $\\{ \\mathbf{v}_2, \\mathbf{v}_3 \\}$ is linearly independent" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(4{v}_{1})+{x}_{2}(5{v}_{2})+{x}_{3}{v}_{3} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4{x}_{1}){v}_{1}+(5{x}_{2}){v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\{ \\mathbf{v}_1, \\mathbf{v}_2, \\mathbf{v}_3\\}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is $x_1=x_2=x_3=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n\\{ 4\\mathbf{v}_1, 5\\mathbf{v}_2, \\mathbf{v}_3\\}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n1 \\cdot \\mathbf{0} + 0 \\cdot \\mathbf{v}_1 + 0 \\cdot (2\\mathbf{v}_2) = \\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, $x_1\\mathbf{0}+x_2\\mathbf{v}_1+x_3(2\\mathbf{v}_2)=\\mathbf{0}$ has a non-zero solution. This means that $\\{ \\mathbf{0}, \\mathbf{v}_1, 2\\mathbf{v}_2 \\}$ is linearly dependent. In general, any set containing the zero vector is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $x_1\\mathbf{v}_2+x_2\\mathbf{v}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ must have only the zero solution $x_1=x_2=0.$  If this equation has a non-zero solution, $a \\cdot \\mathbf{v}_2 + b \\cdot \\mathbf{v}_3=\\mathbf{0},$ then we obtain\n\n$$\n0 \\cdot \\mathbf{v}_1 + a \\cdot \\mathbf{v}_2 + b \\cdot \\mathbf{v}_3 = \\mathbf{0},\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that $\\{ \\mathbf{v}_1, \\mathbf{v}_2, \\mathbf{v}_3\\}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "486cc512-416b-5eac-8964-1a87d533de72" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f80098e5-c2a3-5103-b8f7-876669933d80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448560} {:answer/id #uuid "ce06eac4-88fc-59f1-aeed-a9570958c3d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce06eac4-88fc-59f1-aeed-a9570958c3d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448561} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca230da8-b4e3-5957-a58e-87a045aa03fc" :answer-field/key "${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1},$ ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8c84bb6-a225-5b6c-84dd-f8e1762e2079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448562} {:answer/id #uuid "aa5940ef-ca7b-571b-a904-d308491f9065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8c84bb6-a225-5b6c-84dd-f8e1762e2079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448562} :answer-field/id #uuid "89c1aad6-5394-59ab-b08f-f5e57e86538d" :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449321} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ef425c5-4ceb-5423-9e32-2075e69c60fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448564} {:answer/id #uuid "dc554d18-e7a6-53eb-837d-054067497ae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ef425c5-4ceb-5423-9e32-2075e69c60fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448564} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b3bbfb7-b885-54f7-b50d-ca6a14d38453" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1d95ba8a-32c3-52ab-a4a0-101091efe61a" :question/math-academy-id "q-35706" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent and ${v}_{4}=3{v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}+5{v}_{3},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1},$ ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}$” is true. Indeed, solving equation ${v}_{4}=3{v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}$ for ${v}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=\\frac{3}{2}{v}_{1}+\\frac{5}{2}{v}_{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}_{4}.\n$$\n\nThis means that ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$” is false. Since ${v}_{4}=3{v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}+5{v}_{3},$ we have that\n\n$$\n3\\cdot {v}_{1}-2\\cdot {v}_{2}+5\\cdot {v}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {v}_{4}=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set” is false. Since ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution, the set ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent set by definition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1},$ ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124910 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ed5c88c-d0c0-57ee-99fa-87a72d0451d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448566} {:answer/id #uuid "28d35889-3b91-5223-a2be-21efd5a65c00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28d35889-3b91-5223-a2be-21efd5a65c00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448567} :answer-field/id #uuid "377c37ad-3613-5ae3-973c-4da168168ec1" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},{v}_{2}+{v}_{3},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449323} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c9d5908-fc75-5ff1-b193-357209acfcf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448568} {:answer/id #uuid "e76beabe-d65a-52ab-9f99-26311bdee584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c9d5908-fc75-5ff1-b193-357209acfcf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448568} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e9b79dc-4830-54d1-aa0f-959891ee38b2" :answer-field/key "${0,{v}_{1},2{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449324} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8445c19-3813-5bcb-8cb5-3c1c5432ecd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448570} {:answer/id #uuid "39deadfe-85bd-599d-8611-51462e049bfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39deadfe-85bd-599d-8611-51462e049bfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448571} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a0c186d-c28e-585b-a01f-b4d45a0738de" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8bba7c53-725c-5edb-a90b-13e8c293c9e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-35758" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},{v}_{2}+{v}_{3},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2}+{v}_{3})+{x}_{3}{v}_{3} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){v}_{2}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{3}){v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},{v}_{2}+{v}_{3},{v}_{3}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “${0,{v}_{1},2{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent” is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot {v}_{1}+0\\cdot (2{v}_{2})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}0+{x}_{2}{v}_{1}+{x}_{3}(2{v}_{2})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${0,{v}_{1},2{v}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. In general, any set containing the zero vector is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Indeed, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0$ must have only the zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$  If this equation has a non-zero solution, $a\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}=0,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\na\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}+0\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},{v}_{2}+{v}_{3},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent”; “${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244007 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0944cb0d-450f-5b67-bc93-59b28498a18d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447808} {:answer/id #uuid "a85e529f-a8db-5ac6-81a3-1e8d0132b63d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a85e529f-a8db-5ac6-81a3-1e8d0132b63d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447809} :answer-field/id #uuid "15427a30-4cc6-5970-9c79-47e051d85769" :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448944} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df078c5f-70c2-5841-b99b-67590073383e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447810} {:answer/id #uuid "c3db958d-e8fc-5686-af9e-9756b7ea4499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3db958d-e8fc-5686-af9e-9756b7ea4499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447811} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8806e66-13da-5591-99c5-a443b1af0cfe" :answer-field/key "${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448945} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fdbe147b-5812-50c9-9ca8-b47ac3535278" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447812} {:answer/id #uuid "c70f83db-3806-5abc-98f0-91a2443fb906" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdbe147b-5812-50c9-9ca8-b47ac3535278" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447812} :answer-field/id #uuid "008c8f90-e157-56b2-90cc-b8fd20ff040b" :answer-field/key "${v}_{3}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d584308b-6723-5e86-a9ec-6146a097d3d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-107042" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly dependent and ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution” is true. Since ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent set, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas a non-zero solution.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$” is true. Indeed, solving equation ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ for ${v}_{4},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{v}_{4}=-\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{4}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{x}_{2}}{{x}_{4}}{v}_{2}-\\frac{{x}_{3}}{{x}_{4}}{v}_{3}.\n$$\n\nMoreover, ${x}_{4}$ can't be zero because then\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nwill have a non-zero solution, which contradicts the fact that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent.\nHence, ${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}.$\n\n- Statement “${v}_{3}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$” is false. Since the set ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent set, the equation \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nhas no non-zero solution. Hence, ${v}_{3}$ is not a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution”; “${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "715baca9-d8a1-5a81-a5f7-9987dd0ebe61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447814} {:answer/id #uuid "54ae8f74-a775-5753-af9d-5aa758e47b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54ae8f74-a775-5753-af9d-5aa758e47b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447815} :answer-field/id #uuid "46861617-3930-5b40-a317-855ebcd8a0fd" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}+{v}_{3},2{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448947} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f4209e6-9877-5337-80c6-621256b8783d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447816} {:answer/id #uuid "e30a7d25-8571-5b68-a654-b26e03cd9e05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e30a7d25-8571-5b68-a654-b26e03cd9e05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447817} :answer-field/id #uuid "bafa262d-3852-5589-8bf2-41b9a0fdf267" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448948} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2710465-fa08-5dce-9ba5-b5da64d4c403" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447818} {:answer/id #uuid "0ff3de92-e2fa-5f0c-b8dc-49743ec38723" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2710465-fa08-5dce-9ba5-b5da64d4c403" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447818} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce7c05ed-038d-5fea-9a49-a7875ca70874" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4ec52379-6b69-5ec0-af4a-1a5b49cab942" :question/math-academy-id "q-107043" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}+{v}_{3},2{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}({v}_{1}+{v}_{3})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2}+{v}_{3})+{x}_{3}(2{v}_{3}) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}){v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}+{v}_{3},2{v}_{3}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Indeed, ${x}_{1}{v}_{2}+{x}_{2}{v}_{3}=0$ must have only the zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$  If this equation has a non-zero solution, $a\\cdot {v}_{2}+b\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\n0\\cdot {v}_{1}+a\\cdot {v}_{2}+b\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent” is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot {v}_{1}+1\\cdot {v}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot ({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. In general, any set containing the zero vector is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}+{v}_{3},2{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent”; “${{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "777c64dc-834c-5340-8186-d7fddd2c888a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447820} {:answer/id #uuid "4b6fa1e7-6e00-53aa-84f3-127c952199e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b6fa1e7-6e00-53aa-84f3-127c952199e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447821} :answer-field/id #uuid "834817a5-50c1-530a-be77-2d14fc127805" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1}-{v}_{3},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3}}$ is linearly  independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448950} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0679cae2-d9d9-51ff-b74c-918d4df92c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447822} {:answer/id #uuid "01c77d60-d0ae-5c48-b0af-0c70ea08f222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0679cae2-d9d9-51ff-b74c-918d4df92c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447822} :answer-field/id #uuid "814b088b-03c2-50e2-92e9-c2c38e58f784" :answer-field/key "${0,{v}_{1},-{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448951} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67fa5d24-753f-5219-82b0-70ca7af18650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447824} {:answer/id #uuid "7ec0ce26-4bc7-57c5-9562-50824a1bec0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67fa5d24-753f-5219-82b0-70ca7af18650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447824} :answer-field/id #uuid "048ce3e7-4e91-5bdc-94ae-0dcff0516eac" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c7243a9b-252c-5b36-9021-bf96acea16e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-107044" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1}-{v}_{3},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3}}$ is linearly  independent” is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}({v}_{1}-{v}_{3})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2}-{v}_{3}) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}-({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ -({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}) &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “${0,{v}_{1},-{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent” is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot {v}_{1}+0\\cdot (-{v}_{2})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}0+{x}_{2}{v}_{1}+{x}_{3}(-{v}_{2})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${0,{v}_{1},-{v}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. In general, any set containing the zero vector is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent” is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n1\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+1\\cdot ({v}_{2}-{v}_{1})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{1}}$  is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${{v}_{1}-{v}_{3},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3}}$ is linearly  independent” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244010 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecb71f2b-1000-56b3-bbe6-687b5d590f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447826} {:answer/id #uuid "ad3ee093-657e-5024-8fec-edfa97116b86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad3ee093-657e-5024-8fec-edfa97116b86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447827} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7a813e9-004c-5ceb-a7af-219f8f34da4b" :answer-field/key "${2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},2{v}_{2}-{v}_{1},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448953} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "daca64d4-1f39-5df2-bd12-569ab51b1741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447828} {:answer/id #uuid "91ce4987-96cc-5f80-bf18-867e10fb8c81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "daca64d4-1f39-5df2-bd12-569ab51b1741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447828} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a921d78-ac20-53d2-890f-ca83357fa944" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448954} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87a72c77-5b62-5c9c-8d2c-dce3236ea071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447830} {:answer/id #uuid "505c537f-ba45-5f50-8c2c-f79530d5a17d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "505c537f-ba45-5f50-8c2c-f79530d5a17d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447831} :answer-field/id #uuid "39119c3c-0c5e-55b4-aa93-6b38654a8ce2" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "24ab3e85-383c-51f5-887f-f697f1697031" :question/math-academy-id "q-107045" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},2{v}_{2}-{v}_{1},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}(2{v}_{2}-{v}_{1})+{x}_{3}{v}_{3} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}){v}_{1}+({x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}){v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},2{v}_{2}-{v}_{1},{v}_{3}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent” is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot {v}_{1}+0\\cdot {v}_{2}+1\\cdot (-{v}_{1})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}(-{v}_{1})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},-{v}_{1}}$  is linearly dependent. In general, any set containing the zero vector is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Indeed, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{3}=0$ must have only the zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Indeed,  if this equation has a non-zero solution, $a\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\na\\cdot {v}_{1}+0\\cdot {v}_{2}+b\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},2{v}_{2}-{v}_{1},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent”; “${{v}_{1},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1b10e9b-bcf4-5130-85fc-49053cfefdbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447832} {:answer/id #uuid "475086cf-f02f-5e8a-a4a2-fa006f64dc42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "475086cf-f02f-5e8a-a4a2-fa006f64dc42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447833} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa301ff6-54cb-598d-bef1-558bf2aba10f" :answer-field/key "${2{v}_{1},-3{v}_{2},4{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448956} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a60576b-e768-5815-9199-10025a9ffb26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447834} {:answer/id #uuid "3c33f922-fd87-5120-a935-f4f1b6089257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a60576b-e768-5815-9199-10025a9ffb26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447834} :answer-field/id #uuid "c97d3d50-a922-51ec-9905-e992f040dac9" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},2{v}_{1}-3{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448957} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4854c555-72a3-55eb-8878-f93699e6e4ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447836} {:answer/id #uuid "e5fb77dc-2d83-5c4c-afe5-7ba222ae8083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5fb77dc-2d83-5c4c-afe5-7ba222ae8083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447837} :answer-field/id #uuid "230a8bc2-029d-5dd9-b388-e30b57477b91" :answer-field/key "${-{v}_{1},-{v}_{2},-{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "931e27f9-e2c3-59ee-b477-76a2f89436c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-107048" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${2{v}_{1},-3{v}_{2},4{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2{v}_{1})+{x}_{2}(-3{v}_{2})+{x}_{3}(4{v}_{3}) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}_{1}){v}_{1}+(-3{x}_{2}){v}_{2}+(4{x}_{3}){v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{2{v}_{1},-3{v}_{2},4{v}_{3}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},2{v}_{1}-3{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent” is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n(-2)\\cdot {v}_{1}+3\\cdot {v}_{2}+1\\cdot (2{v}_{1}-3{v}_{2})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}(2{v}_{1}-3{v}_{2})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},2{v}_{1}-3{v}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement “${-{v}_{1},-{v}_{2},-{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Indeed, suppose\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(-{v}_{1})+{x}_{2}(-{v}_{2})+{x}_{3}(-{v}_{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, implies that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-{x}_{1}){v}_{1}+(-{x}_{2}){v}_{2}+(-{x}_{3}){v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,  since ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, it\nmust be ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$  Therefore, the set \n${-{v}_{1},-{v}_{2},-{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${2{v}_{1},-3{v}_{2},4{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent”; “${-{v}_{1},-{v}_{2},-{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329729 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9aa7e7a-8ec0-5ba0-bf53-464cee37bf90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451369} {:answer/id #uuid "30ea5b39-4d55-5079-a6a1-8b5632101d8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9aa7e7a-8ec0-5ba0-bf53-464cee37bf90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451369} :answer-field/id #uuid "f20f6232-94aa-56b0-ba07-28575864e357" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452532} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9fff169-7d2d-5e8f-aa19-b279b7edb09b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451371} {:answer/id #uuid "840be9e1-e201-5c43-80de-26e479a9452c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9fff169-7d2d-5e8f-aa19-b279b7edb09b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451371} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c4c01e1-7882-56f1-a506-19f45fa661b8" :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452533} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd17d168-cd11-5c94-ad0d-d1984bff165d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451373} {:answer/id #uuid "20339164-524f-5900-ab66-5ffccc12418f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20339164-524f-5900-ab66-5ffccc12418f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451374} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e33abb9-a883-5fa6-8001-bfd2368cc29e" :answer-field/key "${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8990a76e-d7f0-501d-8a23-d23acd1f20ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-43786" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set and \n${v}_{1}={v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}-{v}_{4},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set” is false. Since ${v}_{1}={v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}-{v}_{4},$ we have that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot {v}_{1}+(-1)\\cdot {v}_{2}+(-5)\\cdot {v}_{3}+1\\cdot {v}_{4}=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution and the set ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent by definition.\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$” is false.  Since ${v}_{1}={v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}-{v}_{4},$ the equation ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$” is true. Since ${v}_{1}={v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}-{v}_{4},$ we have that\n\n$$\n{v}_{4}={v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}-{v}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThat is, ${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329740 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71f22ab4-c4a5-502a-87f2-77057b0a8bac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451375} {:answer/id #uuid "24f36ec2-6bfa-5409-9d77-f02ebce02bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24f36ec2-6bfa-5409-9d77-f02ebce02bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451376} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f821a04-b96f-56c7-b808-1c064e7b598e" :answer-field/key "${v}_{3}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452535} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b84ff211-ba60-513c-8d51-316b589c1b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451377} {:answer/id #uuid "baa1b90a-bf7e-502d-9cc2-4ad14bcca6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b84ff211-ba60-513c-8d51-316b589c1b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451377} :answer-field/id #uuid "3538bb0a-6213-5f28-a889-384259878e28" :answer-field/key "${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452536} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8718fe10-dc8a-592d-9d40-03f1b228e7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451379} {:answer/id #uuid "e5b677d6-f86f-5b86-8f6d-5f8acde3f926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8718fe10-dc8a-592d-9d40-03f1b228e7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451379} :answer-field/id #uuid "12eb8309-8be1-570a-96c3-7246a920b7d8" :answer-field/key "${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d0d14302-1a26-551e-8f3a-e3f476256916" :question/math-academy-id "q-43827" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set and ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},\\text{ }{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent one, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{3}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}$” is true. Since ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent set, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas a non-zero solution. Moreover, ${x}_{3}$ can't be zero because then\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nwill have a non-zero solution and that's a contradiction as ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent.\nTherefore, from ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{v}_{3}=-\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{3}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{x}_{2}}{{x}_{3}}{v}_{2}-\\frac{{x}_{4}}{{x}_{3}}{v}_{4}.\n$$\n\nThis means that ${v}_{3}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement “${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$” is false. Since ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set, ${v}_{4}$ can not be a linear combination of other vectors.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{4}$” is false. Since ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set, ${v}_{2}$ can not be a linear combination of other vectors.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{3}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360493 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "394603d1-4814-5544-9172-11c68e08f316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452065} {:answer/id #uuid "7bda3b4f-9061-5a39-9045-d26cb78a9944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bda3b4f-9061-5a39-9045-d26cb78a9944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452066} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ffd1df2-f972-5161-a28f-449c584cfb74" :answer-field/key "${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1},$ ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452880} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "318ff92c-73e9-5ee0-aeee-1b2cedad0cd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452067} {:answer/id #uuid "ae733f27-a24e-5cc3-8aa6-a1078d7f759d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae733f27-a24e-5cc3-8aa6-a1078d7f759d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452068} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b957d62-15d8-5a0c-b43b-457d4dc9340a" :answer-field/key "${x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452881} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4e56851-d518-5ff4-9d71-1b336b27e4d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452069} {:answer/id #uuid "8b82d603-c5a1-5823-83d6-0e73228483f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4e56851-d518-5ff4-9d71-1b336b27e4d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452069} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfc426ed-bae3-552f-92fc-a3f6702bf682" :answer-field/key "$\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\}$ is a linearly independent set" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452882}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0b4abe9a-af7a-5741-a378-7c07564b4cd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-94776" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\in V.$ Given that $\\{{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\}$ is linearly independent and ${v}_{1}=2{v}_{2}-{v}_{3}+{v}_{4},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1},$ ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}$” is true. Indeed, solving equation ${v}_{1}=2{v}_{2}-{v}_{3}+{v}_{4},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{v}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{v}_{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}_{4}.\n$$\n\nThis means that ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$” is true. Since $\\{{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\}$ is linearly independent, we have that\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0.$\n\n- Statement “$\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\}$ is a linearly independent set” is false. Since ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution, the set $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\}$ is a linearly dependent by definition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1},$ ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}$”; “${x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360494 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a21705a3-5a29-5f73-9072-c0a63af32911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452071} {:answer/id #uuid "3da1bd10-2484-51b1-9c33-1bb7f771c811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3da1bd10-2484-51b1-9c33-1bb7f771c811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452072} :answer-field/id #uuid "24c54d39-d8cb-5afc-8267-ab1e8cc75f8e" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452883} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1be81f08-17d0-5336-96ef-6bed2c7e7aa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452073} {:answer/id #uuid "cc44823a-b6fa-5661-989c-e371c7a18718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1be81f08-17d0-5336-96ef-6bed2c7e7aa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452073} :answer-field/id #uuid "930bab5e-8c86-58eb-a0d6-ec0c808c8686" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20dafd89-d5eb-572c-be39-5955d431ef9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452075} {:answer/id #uuid "706da707-f77b-5e37-b9f4-2828f578de41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "706da707-f77b-5e37-b9f4-2828f578de41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452076} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ac026ce-b6d8-5e03-9f40-19c298b1d5ba" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cbf9c53e-84bd-5e5c-95e0-1c3b39f57ad9" :question/math-academy-id "q-94779" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}({v}_{1}+{v}_{3})+{x}_{3}{v}_{2} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){v}_{1}+({x}_{1}+{x}_{3}){v}_{2}+{x}_{2}{v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent” is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+1\\cdot ({v}_{2}-{v}_{1})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2}-{v}_{1})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Indeed, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0$ must have only the zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$  If this equation has a non-zero solution, $a\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}=0,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\na\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}+0\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${{v}_{1}+{v}_{2},{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent”; “${{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360495 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eac94ca6-8049-5111-bc2a-d45e4fdc270b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452077} {:answer/id #uuid "c37d0316-ca6b-5c8e-8310-66a45ba19f96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eac94ca6-8049-5111-bc2a-d45e4fdc270b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452077} :answer-field/id #uuid "a63aee5d-829b-5d33-a17d-51582d4066df" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3},{v}_{3}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452886} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91df8c2f-9a86-530d-bd0c-56de10c94d19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452079} {:answer/id #uuid "599286cc-3c8f-59a0-93da-f7c7c1e6ae7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "599286cc-3c8f-59a0-93da-f7c7c1e6ae7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452080} :answer-field/id #uuid "55f26d78-2b79-501b-83ef-2c928e846e37" :answer-field/key "${2{v}_{1},{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8756b124-e725-5b72-83a2-827421bf6e79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452081} {:answer/id #uuid "ecbe3332-ad2a-5807-bec7-0421f2a405f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8756b124-e725-5b72-83a2-827421bf6e79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452081} :answer-field/id #uuid "21d0f96f-4afc-5e0e-8aeb-00020a2bc184" :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "db8c1e1e-2555-50dd-bb83-7ef5667f1f43" :question/math-academy-id "q-94781" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3},{v}_{3}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent” is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+1\\cdot ({v}_{2}-{v}_{3})+1\\cdot ({v}_{3}-{v}_{1})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2}-{v}_{3})+{x}_{3}({v}_{3}-{v}_{1})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3},{v}_{3}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement “${2{v}_{1},{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2{v}_{1})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2})+{x}_{3}(3{v}_{3}) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}_{1}){v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+(3{x}_{3}){v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{2{v}_{1},{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent” is false.  If ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0$ has a non-zero solution, $a\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}=0,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\na\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}+0\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${2{v}_{1},{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373540 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6429683f-31e8-587f-9bb6-943f9c82808e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453204} {:answer/id #uuid "4cdec651-22d0-5cdc-8ed3-7bdaf0df5030" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6429683f-31e8-587f-9bb6-943f9c82808e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453204} :answer-field/id #uuid "9880c020-21e3-5d95-a6ac-b7dd403e79c4" :answer-field/key "$\\{{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3},{v}_{1}-{v}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454352} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d39f87e-17b4-54ca-8e3d-abd7a0fd1e75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453206} {:answer/id #uuid "cf8f6a1e-a71e-5ccf-b95b-576393c72cb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf8f6a1e-a71e-5ccf-b95b-576393c72cb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453207} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d0c4844-ac6c-5d61-8dbe-13c93d0977ea" :answer-field/key "$\\{{v}_{1},2{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454353} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03783e7e-3525-506f-8dfe-fc9257d75eff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453208} {:answer/id #uuid "f408e24a-eb89-5177-aca3-74153b203cb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03783e7e-3525-506f-8dfe-fc9257d75eff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453208} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3d35fc4-4a66-5588-9bb4-1ae54e82809d" :answer-field/key "$\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},0\\}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3e3aa161-9904-5811-8bd5-9983d559a3c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-107047" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “$\\{{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3},{v}_{1}-{v}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent” is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+1\\cdot ({v}_{2}-{v}_{3})+(-1)\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{3})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2}-{v}_{3})+{x}_{3}({v}_{1}-{v}_{3})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that $\\{{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3},{v}_{1}-{v}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement “$\\{{v}_{1},2{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent” is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}(2{v}_{2})+{x}_{3}(3{v}_{3}) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+3{x}_{3}{v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n\\{{v}_{1},2{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}\\}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “$\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},0\\}$ is linearly independent” is false. Indeed, notice that \n\n$$\n0\\cdot {v}_{1}+0\\cdot {v}_{2}+1\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}0=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},0\\}$ is linearly dependent. In general, any set containing the zero vector is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$\\{{v}_{1},2{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407778 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d8c3ee6-fd37-5cb0-b0ab-80e7a7cca090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454166} {:answer/id #uuid "cd824f2a-c47c-53a0-be26-c6bd74e52573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd824f2a-c47c-53a0-be26-c6bd74e52573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454167} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b613250-bfe0-5d10-933a-62b1f7c0e186" :answer-field/key "${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454833} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e25a9185-5eae-580c-a0fe-a1704d681147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value 