 are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$” is true. Since ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent set, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas a non-zero solution. Moreover, ${x}_{1}$ can't be zero because then\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nwill have a non-zero solution and that's a contradiction as ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent.\nTherefore, from ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=-\\frac{{x}_{2}}{{x}_{1}}{v}_{2}-\\frac{{x}_{3}}{{x}_{1}}{v}_{3}-\\frac{{x}_{4}}{{x}_{1}}{v}_{4}.\n$$\n\nThis means that ${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$, ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$” is false. Since ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set, ${v}_{2}$ can not be a linear combination of other vectors.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}+{v}_{3}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}$” is false. Since ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set, ${v}_{3}$ can not be a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}.$ As a result ${v}_{2}+{v}_{3}$ can't be written as combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}$ too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415061 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c31adaa2-aedb-51ee-98cc-f5a5cb7cb242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453874} {:answer/id #uuid "063facdd-b115-5116-95a9-caa5bdab8f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 